1
00:06:52,941 --> 00:06:58,941
The sun dawned bloodied... two great armies met face to face... and the
earth trembled to the sound of the Zulu death chant!

2
00:13:45,882 --> 00:13:51,882
Zulu Dawn is a adventure, drama, history film directed by Douglas Hickox.

3
00:20:38,823 --> 00:20:44,823
In 1879, the British suffer a great loss at the Battle of
Isandlwana due to incompetent leadership.

4
00:27:31,764 --> 00:27:37,764
Col. Anthony Durnford, played by Burt Lancaster.

5
00:34:24,705 --> 00:34:30,705
Lt. Vereker, played by Simon Ward.

6
00:41:17,647 --> 00:41:23,647
Colonel Pulleine, played by Denholm Elliott.

7
00:48:10,588 --> 00:48:16,588
QSM Bloomfield, played by Peter Vaughan.

8
00:55:03,529 --> 00:55:09,529
Lt. Melvill, played by James Faulkner.

9
01:01:56,470 --> 01:02:02,470
Lt. Coghill, played by Christopher Cazenove.

10
01:08:49,411 --> 01:08:55,411
Zulu Dawn is a 1979 American adventure war film directed by Douglas
Hickox and written by Anthony Storey and Cy Endfield.

11
01:15:42,352 --> 01:15:48,352
It is based on Endfield's book of the same name about the historical Battle of
Isandlwana in 1879 between British and Zulu forces in South Africa.

12
01:22:35,294 --> 01:22:41,294
Zulu Dawn features an ensemble cast led by Burt Lancaster, 
Peter O'Toole, Simon Ward, and Nigel Davenport.

13
01:29:28,235 --> 01:29:34,235
Chronologically it precedes the smaller Battle of Rorke's Drift,
which also had opposing British and Zulu forces.

14
01:36:21,176 --> 01:36:27,176
Zulu (1964) was a film about the latter battle.

15
01:43:14,117 --> 01:43:20,117
The film explores themes of fight, british
empire, victory, prequel, battlefield.

16
01:50:07,058 --> 01:50:13,058
The tone is emotional.
